From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:08:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add the X-DKIM2-Info debug header

Every Message-Instance Sympa adds (m=1 at ingress, m=N at egress) is
accompanied by an X-DKIM2-Info field directly above it, in the
draft-gondwana-dkim2-debug-header-01 form: a tag-list in the DKIM2
syntax, every tag followed by ";", recording the draft implemented, the
repository and date of the implementation, the software, the action
("mi-m=<N>"), and the count and ordered names of the header fields that
went into the hash. It exists so an interop problem can be diagnosed from
the message alone. The value is folded only after a ";" or ",", never
inside a token, and it is outside the header hash by the spec's X- rule.
Where the chain is stripped (anonymous lists, resends from the archive)
X-DKIM2-Info goes with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
